"Getsome" <n...@no.com> wrote:

> I am playing Slash'Em in windows but the tiles are
> too small to see at 1280x1028
> Is there a way to get larger tiles?

Tiles exist (in the "Absurd" tile set) in sizes up
to 128x128, though I've never heard of them being
successfully used that big; which size are you using
now, and on what platform (non-standard tiles
availability is platform dependent)?

It's trivially easy to take a 32x32 tile set and
pixel replicate it bigger with some free image
processing tool like GIMP.

I'm personally using a scaled set (to 15x30) I made
out of the 20x40 tiles available here:

http://www.olywa.net/cook/nhack.htm

which fits my 1280x800 screen really well, and which
tiles are a nice compromise between text and images
hard to explain until you try it. I especially enjoy
how well the dungeon layout tiles are crafted,
giving really, really nice "dungeony" level images.

At 15x30, those tiles just fit a whole level on my
screen at once.

